{"id": "msg_1032", "user_name": "meme-benchmark", "session_id": "d038f2e6-8549-4deb-bc66-314776a45cd0", "role": "assistant", "message": "<div class=\"markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light\"><p>To get all the completed tasks from the Todoist API using Python and the requests library, you will need to include the <code>completed_since</code> parameter in your request to the sync endpoint.\nThis parameter can be a unix timestamp or a date string in the format <code>YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ</code>, and it will return all completed tasks that were completed since that timestamp or date.</p><p>Here's an example of how you can use the requests library to get all completed tasks from the Todoist API:</p><pre><div class=\"bg-black mb-4 rounded-md\"><div class=\"flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans\"><button class=\"flex ml-auto gap-2\"><svg stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4\" height=\"1em\" width=\"1em\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2\"></path><rect x=\"8\" y=\"2\" width=\"8\" height=\"4\" rx=\"1\" ry=\"1\"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class=\"p-4 overflow-y-auto\"><code class=\"!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> requests\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> json\n\napi_token = <span class=\"hljs-string\">'YOUR_API_TOKEN'</span>\nheaders = {<span class=\"hljs-string\">'Authorization'</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">f'Bearer <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{api_token}</span>'</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">'Content-Type'</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">'application/json'</span>}\n\ndata = json.dumps({<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"completed_since\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"now\"</span>})\nresponse = requests.post(<span class=\"hljs-string\">'https://api.todoist.com/sync/v8/sync'</span>, headers=headers, data=data)\n\ntasks = response.json()[<span class=\"hljs-string\">'items'</span>]\ncompleted_tasks = [task <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> task <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> tasks <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> task[<span class=\"hljs-string\">'checked'</span>] == <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]\n\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(completed_tasks)\n</code></div></div></pre><p>This example uses the <code>post</code> method to send a request to the sync endpoint, passing a json payload with the <code>completed_since</code> parameter set to <code>\"now\"</code>.\nThe response is a json object with all the task items, the script filter the completed tasks by checking the 'checked' attribute of each task, and print it.</p><p>You can also set the completed_since to a specific date and time in the past, to get the completed task only from that date.</p><pre><div class=\"bg-black mb-4 rounded-md\"><div class=\"flex items-center relative text-gray-200 bg-gray-800 px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans\"><button class=\"flex ml-auto gap-2\"><svg stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4\" height=\"1em\" width=\"1em\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2\"></path><rect x=\"8\" y=\"2\" width=\"8\" height=\"4\" rx=\"1\" ry=\"1\"></rect></svg>Copy code</button></div><div class=\"p-4 overflow-y-auto\"><code class=\"!whitespace-pre-wrap hljs language-python\">data = json.dumps({<span class=\"hljs-string\">\"completed_since\"</span>: <span class=\"hljs-string\">\"2022-12-01T00:00:00Z\"</span>})\n</code></div></div></pre><p>Please check Todoist API documentation for more information about the available parameters and options.</p></div>", "timestamp": "2023-03-12T13:14:00+00:00", "score": 1.0, "co