{"id": "msg_1016", "user_name": "meme-benchmark", "session_id": "d038f2e6-8549-4deb-bc66-314776a45cd0", "role": "user", "message": "Several people are trying to run a Notion page where they write how to use GPT. One article contains one usage method. I try to tag each post to make it easy to find information. The contents of the articles posted so far are as follows. Please read below and create appropriate tags to attach to these articles. Tags should not be too specific or too generic. The content of each article consists of a command (example) and an explanation of the command.\n\n1. Assign roles\nCommand: [You are a talented analyst at a top-tier market research firm, a graduate of Harvard Business School. Coach me to create content that connects with C-level executives at B2B SaaS companies. What open-ended questions do I ask? Prioritize uncommon, expert advice.]\nDescription: Grant ChatGPT to assume the expert role\ndrive better answers\n\n2. Waiting for commands\nCommand: [Answer \"OK\" to confirm and I will paste the next text.]\nDescription: ChatGPT is waiting without answering.\nJust add it at the end.\n(simple version)\n\n3. Step-by-step ordering\nCommand: [Step by Step]\nExplanation: It is often used when logic such as mathematics is required.\n\n4. Emphasize\nCommand : [- !IMPORTANT : ~~ ]\nDescription: Create priorities by setting the most needed features.\n\n5. Get to the point\nCommand: [Return only the main response. Remove pre-text and post-text.]\nDescription: Eliminate unnecessary introductions and conclusions.\nIt has the effect of reducing tokens.\n\n6. Storytelling writing\nCommand: [Voice and style guide: Makes use of persuasive tone, making use of rhetorical questions, and storytelling to engage readers. Use metaphors, analogies and other literary devices to make points more relatable and memorable. Write in a way that is both informative and entertaining.]\nDescription: Increases the quality of writing.\nThe core keywords are \"Storytelling\".\nStorytelling is all you need.\n\n7. Format Markdown\nCommand: [Format your response using markdown. Use headings, subheadings, bullet points, and bold to organize the information.]\nDescription: Organize your document in the form of a table of contents (with bullets)\n\n8. Organize prompts (my questions)\nCommand: [Can you please rephrase the question and provide an answer accordingly?]\nDescription: Cleans up my prompts.\nIt produces better results by giving results in more detailed steps.\n\n9. Write in a specific writer's style\nCommand: [Emulate Ernest Hemingway's writing style.]\nDescription: Enter the name of the desired artist.\nIn the same vein, using 'true stories' improves the quality of your writing.\n\n10. Continue listening to the disconnected answer\nCommand: [Keep going]\n[continue]\n[Keep going from exactly where you left]\nDescription: When the answer is cut off due to its length, you can continue listening.\n\nWhen used in a situation where code is being written, content may be omitted in the middle.\nIn this case, it can be solved by giving additional instructions later.\n(Start with “a specific line of code”, keep going from exactly where you left, etc..)\n\n11. Code writing tips\nCommand : [ When you write the code, in order to reduce errors, consider the function name, variable name, number of arguments and parameters, libraries, etc. ]\nDescription: This is a function to reduce errors in code.\nAdd and edit necessary conditions to use.\n\n12. Serving Code Errors\nCommand : [ below is my full code. ]\n\n…\n\n[ and that code returns ]\nDescription: Full code first.\nAfter that, it gives the error message of that code.\n\n13. Get feedback on your questions\nCommand: [ Give me feedback on my question ]\nDescription: You can get feedback on your question level.\n\n14. Default Prompt\nCommand : [ please answer the #Topic following the conditions below.\nTopic : [keyword]\nLength : around 2000 words\nFormat : markdown\nAnswer me in Korean/English\nIncludes titile, subtitles and detail descriptions\nFor Audience: 15 years old students\nContent Goal: Blog (Press Release, Report)\nWriting style : Financial Professional (Steve Jobs) ]\nDescription: A hearty default prompt.\nModify and use according to each condition.\nAnswer in English.지금 번역하기", "timestamp": "2023-03-08T19:22:00+00:00", "score": 1.0, "context": [{"role": "user", "timestamp": "2023-03-08T19:22:00+00:00", "content": "Several people are trying to run a Notion page where they write how to use GPT. One article contains one usage method. I try to tag each post to make it easy to find information. The contents of the articles posted so far are as follows. Please read below and create appropriate tags to attach to these articles. Tags should not be too specific or too generic. The content of each article consists of a command (example) and an explanation of the command.\n\n1. Assign roles\nCommand: [You are a talented analyst at a top-tier market research firm, a graduate of Harvard Business School. Coach me to create content that connects with C-level executives at B2B SaaS companies. What open-ended questions do I ask? Prioritize uncommon, expert advice.]\nDescription: Grant ChatGPT to assume the expert role\ndrive better answers\n\n2. Waiting for commands\nCommand: [Answer \"OK\" to confirm and I will paste the next text.]\nDescription: ChatGPT is waiting without answering.\nJust add it at the end.\n(simple version)\n\n3. Step-by-step ordering\nCommand: [Step by Step]\nExplanation: It is often used when logic such as mathematics is required.\n\n4. Emphasize\nCommand : [- !IMPORTANT : ~~ ]\nDescription: Create priorities by setting the most needed features.\n\n5. Get to the point\nCommand: [Return only the main response. Remove pre-text and post-text.]\nDescription: Eliminate unnecessary introductions and conclusions.\nIt has the effect of reducing tokens.\n\n6. Storytelling writing\nCommand: [Voice and style guide: Makes use of persuasive tone, mak